Package: perturbMatch
Type: Package
Title: Match Transcriptomics Signatures to Single-Gene Perturbation References
Version: 0.99.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jamie", "Soul", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jamie.soul@liverpool.ac.uk", 
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2255-6459")),
    person("Versus Arthritis", role = "fnd")
  )
Description: Matches a query transcriptomics signature against a reference
    database of single-gene perturbation signatures, ranking the perturbations
    whose expression response most resembles the query and so nominating the
    regulators most likely to drive the observed change. Query signatures
    derived from a differential expression result are scored using cosine,
    GSEA and signed-Jaccard similarity metrics. Reference databases are
    supplied as HDF5-backed SummarizedExperiment objects for memory-efficient
    handling of large perturbation collections, and helper functions rank and
    visualise the best-matching regulators.
Depends: R (>= 4.6.0)
